{"term":"advance","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fa608a5075f8864a74","definition":"To promote or advantage.","example":"Some see it as in effect the end of the Syrian uprising that began with peaceful protests against Assad’s police state in 2011, with opposition fighters working to advance Turkey’s interests at the expense of the revolution’s goals.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["improve","assign"],"antonyms":["regress","retract","retreat"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["advanceable","advancement","advance the ball","advancingly","advancive","unadvancing","readvance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7bceca49bb179970be","definition":"To move forward in space or time.","example":"Whence and what art thou, execrable shape, / That dar'st, though grim and terrible, advance / Thy miscreated front athwart my way / To yonder gates?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["improve","assign"],"antonyms":["regress","retract","retreat"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["advanceable","advancement","advance the ball","advancingly","advancive","unadvancing","readvance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2799c4c49202a002aa","definition":"To raise, be raised.","example":"The fringed Curtaines of thine eyes aduance.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["heighten"],"antonyms":["regress","retract","retreat"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["advanceable","advancement","advance the ball","advancingly","advancive","unadvancing","readvance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/advance#English","license":"CC-B